      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 2.07,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "Angular has two main ways it gives you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 8.52,
          "en": "when it comes to handling forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.52,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "And of course, as you saw already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "you don't need to use either of these two ways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "or at least you don't have to use all the features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "these two different main approaches give you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "because we have been able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "to handle user input in earlier course sections already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 32.72,
          "en": "without knowing anything about these two main ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.88,
          "end": 37.2,
          "en": "But as you're building more complex Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 40.14,
          "en": "and potentially all the more complex forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.14,
          "end": 45,
          "en": "or as you want to do more than just extract values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "you might be interested in using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "one of these two main ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "And when it comes to these two approaches Angular gives you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 59.583,
          "en": "we, for example, have the template-driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.48,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "The idea here is that you set up your forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "with help of the component templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 70.05,
          "en": "and you register inputs with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.05,
          "end": 73.95,
          "en": "so that it is aware of them with help of your templates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.95,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "so directly in the templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "And therefore, this approach, as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 82.23,
          "en": "is relatively easy to get started with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.23,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "but it can also face some limitations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "or it may get trickier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 93.12,
          "en": "as you're building more complex forms, though ultimately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.12,
          "end": 95.28,
          "en": "as always, it is of course up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.28,
          "end": 97.923,
          "en": "whether you want to use this approach or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "The alternative about which you will also learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "in this section would be reactive forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 110.34,
          "en": "where you set up your form structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.34,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "in your TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 116.37,
          "en": "and you then just link that to the template elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.37,
          "end": 120.57,
          "en": "so that Angular knows which input element in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.57,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "is related to which control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 126.12,
          "en": "that was set up in the TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.12,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "And therefore, as you will also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "the setup step can be a bit more complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 136.77,
          "en": "can require more code, and is a bit more verbose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.77,
          "end": 141.75,
          "en": "But the advantage can be that handling more complex forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.75,
          "end": 146.613,
          "en": "may be easier than when using that template-driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "But of course with that, this is all still relatively vague",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "and unclear, I'd imagine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 157.82999999999998,
          "en": "So therefore, let's simply dive right in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.82999999999998,
          "end": 161.28,
          "en": "and let's start with template-driven forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.28,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "and let's explore how you would manage this form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "with help of this template-driven forms approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 171.663,
          "en": "Angular offers you.",
          "zh": ""
